pst-marble
https://ctan.org/pkg/pst-marble
Copyright 2018, 2019 Aubrey Jaffer. Maintainers: Aubrey Jaffer, Manuel Luque,
and the late Jurgen Gilg.
License: LaTeX Project Public License 1.3c
https://www.latex-project.org/lppl/lppl-1-3c/

Marbler began as a JavaScript reimplementation of this package, and part of
it is a Derived Work under that license:

  - engine.js, Marble._tine, is translated into JavaScript from
    /stylus-deformation in pst-marble.pro, and changed: it applies to outline
    points tick by tick, limits how far each step reaches, and on a repeating
    tank measures distances across the seams.
  - engine.js, the stir and drop motions, and film.js, the radial map close
    to a drop, follow pst-marble's formulas, reworked to apply a little at a
    time. The drop map is also published in Lu, Jaffer, Jin, Zhao and Mao,
    "Mathematical Marbling" (2012).

